self-test: cyclotomic polynomials, divisibility and the levels agree with cases worked by hand; with exponents 0, 1 the count is 4 against 2, so "at most once" would fail and "twice" is met with equality
U: 4000 cases (groups Z^2, Z/2, Z/3, Z/4, Z/6; 0 to 9 elements; K 0 to 4; 0 to 3 systems of values, 1050 of them with none), none against it; the largest ratio met 2.000; equality with fewer than all signings bad in 249
W: 1500 cases (0 to 10 elements, exponents repeated or not and not reduced; k 0 to 3; n' in 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 15), none against it; the largest ratio met 2.000; equality with fewer than all signings bad in 348
